eatening humanity.\\n3. **The Matrix Reloaded** (2003) and **The Matrix Revolutions** (2003) - These sequels to The Matrix offer a similar blend of innovative action sequences, complex sci-fi concepts, and a sprawling narrative.\\n4. **Star Wars: The Last Jedi** (2017) - While not directly comparable to Avengers: Endgame, this Star Wars installment features a similar sense of epic scope, action, and dramatic stakes.\\n5. **Edge of Tomorrow** (2014) - This sci-fi action film, starring Tom Cruise, has a similar sense of fast-paced action, time-traveling, and a desperate battle against an alien threat.\\n6. **War of the Worlds** (2005) - This Steven Spielberg film, based on the H.G. Wells classic, features a similar sense of scope and scale, with a global alien invasion threatening humanity.\\n7. **The Fifth Element** (1997) - This visually stunning sci-fi film, directed by Luc Besson, has a similar sense of action, adventure, and epic scope, set in a futuristic world.\\n8. **I Am Legend** (2007) - This post-apocalyptic thriller, starring Will Smith, features a similar sense of desolate landscapes, action, and a desperate battle for survival against a deadly threat.\\n9. **Geostorm** (2017) - This disaster film, directed by Dean Devlin, has a similar sense of global scope, action, and sci-fi concepts, as a network of satellites designed to control the global climate starts to malfunction.\\n10. **Oblivion** (2013) - This Tom Cruise-starring sci-fi film features a similar sense of action, adventure, and epic scope, set in a post-apocalyptic world where humans are fighting against an alien threat.\\n\\nThese movies offer a mix of action, adventure, and sci-fi elements that fans of Avengers: Endgame tend to enjoy. Keep in mind that while they may not be exact duplicates, they share some similarities with the Marvel epic in terms of scale and scope. \"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': \"Since I just re-watched Avengers: Endgame yesterday, I've been thinking about other movies